摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A deepseek-harness plugin, making your agent evolve in customed git repository.","id":"gh:1341474906","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-evolve-in-git","slug":"Kytolly/dsh-evolve-in-git","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A deepseek-harness plugin, making your agent evolve in customed git repository."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-evolve-in-git"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English · 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Git-backed long-term memory and evolution plugin for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- What it does\n- Install\n- Usage\n- Architecture\n- Data layout\n- Config\n- Harness entry points\n- Brow"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ser half\n- Development\n- Delivery notes\n- License"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"This plugin treats a user-chosen or preconfigured Git repository as the memory store.\nIt can write s"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ession notes, branch-specific records, and reusable skill drafts into that repo, then commit them as"},{"id":"p8s3","text":" ordinary Git history."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The bundle inserts one `dsh-evolve-in-git` row with the plugin defaults.\nLater profile patches can o"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"verride `repoPath`, `repoUrl`, `auth`, and the storage roots."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Natural language"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"You do not need to remember tool names — describe the outcome and the model\nselects the right `evolv"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"e_*` / `memory_*` tool:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| You say (or similar) | The model uses |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| \"Remember: whenever X happens, do Y\" | `evolve_remember` / `memory_save` |\n| \"Any memory about the"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" deploy flow?\" | `evolve_recall` / `memory_search` |\n| \"Read my recent memory history\" | `evolve_tim"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"eline` |\n| \"Turn this warning into a reusable skill\" | `evolve_skill_draft` → `evolve_skill_promote`"},{"id":"p16s4","text":" |\n| \"What is the memory repo's current state?\" | `evolve_status` / `evolve_branches` |\n| \"Undo the "},{"id":"p16s5","text":"last memory commit\" | `evolve_rollback` |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Commands (`/evolve`)"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"For explicit, deterministic control, type `/evolve <subcommand>`:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The full command reference is under Harness entry points."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The package is split into a **framework-free core** and a thin **DSH adapter**:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"- `src/core.ts` (`GitMemoryCore`) is the portability boundary. It depends only on\nNode built-ins and"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" sibling core modules — never on `@deepseek-ai/*` — and\nresolves config from the on-disk file over t"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"he host-provided base.\n- `src/index.ts` (`GitEvolutionService`) is the adapter: it registers Cordis\n"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"tools, the `/evolve` command, the system-prompt section, the skill provider,\nand the config-file rou"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"te, then maps every surface onto `GitMemoryCore`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| Module | Responsibility |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| `src/git.ts` | Spawns `git`: clone/open, status, branch ops, push/fetch, commit, `git mv`, conflic"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ts, rollback. |\n| `src/memory.ts` + `src/memory-index.ts` | Markdown+YAML-frontmatter scanning, a me"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"tadata index cache (HEAD + mtime signature), budgeted recall, timeline. |\n| `src/update.ts` | Versio"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ned update: a new active record plus `supersedes`/`supersededBy`; the old file is never deleted. |\n|"},{"id":"p25s5","text":" `src/forget.ts` | Soft-delete (move to `archiveRoot`) and restore. |\n| `src/privacy.ts` | Sensitive"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"-content detection, sensitivity classification, redaction, export filtering. |\n| `src/skill.ts` | `d"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"rafts/` ↔ `enabled/` skill discovery; promote/demote via `git mv`; bundled-skill sync. |\n| `src/stra"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"tegy.ts` | Slug/sanitize, draft generation from a memory, evolution suggestion, preview. |\n| `src/ha"},{"id":"p25s9","text":"rness.ts` | `/evolve` command normalization/parsing plus help/usage/safety text. |\n| `src/config.ts`"},{"id":"p25s10","text":" + `src/defaults.ts` | Config-file read/write/merge and the plugin defaults. |\n| `src/invariant.ts` "},{"id":"p25s11","text":"| No-op invariant companion (the source of truth is the configured Git repo). |\n| `src/loopback.ts` "},{"id":"p25s12","text":"+ `src/config-route.ts` | Loopback-only `/api/evolve-git/config` route for the config-file editor. |"},{"id":"p25s13","text":"\n| `src/client/` | Browser settings section (`evolve-git` slot) and config-file editor. |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Data layout"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **Memory** — `<repo>/<memoryRoot>/<kind>/<timestamp>-<slug>-<id>.md`, one\nMarkdown file per record"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" with YAML frontmatter (`kind`, `title`, `branch`,\n`source`, `tags`, `createdAt`, `id`, `updatedAt`,"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" `status`, `supersedes`,\n`supersededBy`, `expiresAt`, `sensitivity`) followed by the body.\n- **Skill"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"s** — `<repo>/<skillsRoot>/drafts/<name>/SKILL.md` (promotable) and\n`<repo>/<skillsRoot>/enabled/<na"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"me>/SKILL.md` (discoverable). Promotion is a\n`git mv` between the two, never a copy, so it stays rev"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"ersible and in history.\n- **Archive** — `<repo>/<archiveRoot>/…` (same relative layout as memory);\n`"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"evolve_forget` moves records here so they leave recall/timeline but stay\nrecoverable. `archiveRoot` "},{"id":"p27s8","text":"must remain outside `memoryRoot`."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Config"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"> **Web settings UI (v0.1.4+).** The plugin ships a browser half that registers a\n> first-level **Se"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ttings → 演进记忆** section on the web profile's Settings page\n> (via the `settings.section` slot). The "},{"id":"p29s3","text":"form uses a `SettingsScope` adapter that\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Privacy write gate"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Every memory write passes through the privacy gate (emails, phones, ID cards,\ncredit cards, AWS keys"},{"id":"p31s2","text":", GitHub tokens, private keys, and `password:`-style\nsecrets). `privacyMode` controls the response:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"- `block` - reject the write when sensitive content is detected.\n- `redact` - replace detected fragm"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ents with `<REDACTED>` and store that instead of the plaintext.\n- `ask` (default) - store the conten"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"t as-is and record its `sensitivity` so it can be reviewed and confirmed."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"`evolve_show`/`evolve_export` respect the recorded `sensitivity` level, and\nexports exclude `secret`"},{"id":"p33s2","text":" records by default. Records without a recorded\n`sensitivity` (written before the gate existed) are "},{"id":"p33s3","text":"treated as `secret` so they\nare never accidentally exported."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"The gate covers **memory writes only** (`writeMemoryRecord`/`updateMemory`, i.e.\n`evolve_remember`/`"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"memory_save`/`evolve_update`/`memory_update`). Skill-draft\nwrites (`writeSkillDraft`/`saveSkillDraft"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"FromRecord`) intentionally do **not** go\nthrough the privacy gate in this release; review drafts for"},{"id":"p34s4","text":" secrets before\npromoting them."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"> **Recall scoring.** `evolve_recall`/`memory_search` score a query against record\n> metadata (`titl"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"e`, `kind`, `tags`, `branch`, `source`) only; the body is loaded\n> lazily for the top matches but is"},{"id":"p35s3","text":" not part of the relevance score. The human\n> command `/evolve search <q>` uses the same metadata-in"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"dexed recall, so it\n> returns the same ranked results rather than a different matcher.\n>\n> **Archive"},{"id":"p35s5","text":" constraint.** `archiveRoot` must stay outside `memoryRoot` (the\n> default `.dsh-evolve/archive` doe"},{"id":"p35s6","text":"s). If you point `archiveRoot` inside\n> `memoryRoot`, forgotten records are still scanned and will n"},{"id":"p35s7","text":"int `archiveRoot` inside\n> `memoryRoot`, forgotten records are still scanned and will not disappear."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
